Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:54:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] radeon_hd: enable CRTC VGA mode around BlankCRTC on DCE
 10+

The BlankCRTC table loops until the 5 second AtomBIOS timeout unless
the CRTC's VGA mode is enabled while it runs, as done by Linux in
dce_v11_0_crtc_dpms(). The delay made monitors with several inputs
switch away to another input during boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NqrEBcidivS5BSWVfbLqvu
---
 src/add-ons/accelerants/radeon_hd/display.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/accelerants/radeon_hd/display.cpp b/src/add-ons/accelerants/radeon_hd/display.cpp
index bd47f8e7c0..960dfba09b 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/accelerants/radeon_hd/display.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/accelerants/radeon_hd/display.cpp
@@ -622,7 +622,20 @@ display_crtc_blank(uint8 crtcID, int command)
 	args.usBlackColorGY = 0;
 	args.usBlackColorBCb = 0;
 
+	// On DCE 10+ BlankCRTC waits forever unless VGA mode is enabled on the
+	// CRTC while the table runs (Linux dce_v11_0_crtc_dpms)
+	radeon_shared_info &info = *gInfo->shared_info;
+	register_info* regs = gDisplay[crtcID]->regs;
+	uint32 vgaControl = 0;
+	if (info.dceMajor >= 10) {
+		vgaControl = Read32(OUT, regs->vgaControl) & ~1;
+		Write32(OUT, regs->vgaControl, vgaControl | 1);
+	}
+
 	atom_execute_table(gAtomContext, index, (uint32*)&args);
+
+	if (info.dceMajor >= 10)
+		Write32(OUT, regs->vgaControl, vgaControl);
 }
 
 
